cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the released weights, please cite the paper."
title: "Forget the Data, Keep the Capability: Switchable Unlearning for Retrieval"
abstract: >-
  MoME splits one re-identification backbone into core parameters that preserve retrieval and
  zero-initialized parasitic parameters that carry the full-data knowledge, and trains them under
  gradient isolation so the core never receives a forget-set gradient. Disabling the branch yields
  Core, which satisfies a request to delete a person's training data; enabling it yields Full.
  Honoring a request is a flag flip rather than a retraining run. Forgetting-Rank audits that
  independence in a trained model.
